loat"><label>Table 2</label><caption><title>Upstream regulatory TFs and their regulatory function <italic>&#x0011c;</italic>(<italic>k</italic>) on E2F target genes in cancer cell cycle</title><p>The positive sign implies activations while the negative sign implies inhibitions for each target gene. The magnitudes indicate their regulatory abilities to the downstream target genes.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN-02-223-t002"/></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t3-cin-02-223" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><title>The 152 E2F target genes in the gene regulatory network based on the dynamic regulatory modeling</title><p>The marked signs are the matched E2F target genes found by Elkon et al. (2003).</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><tbody><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">BAIAP2</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">TOP3A</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">ACYP1</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">BIVM</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">ADCK2</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">OGT</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">C20orf55</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">SSR3</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">MED31</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">CDC6<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cin-02-223">*</xref><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn2-cin-02-223">#</xref></td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">FLJ10154</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">FANCG</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">PILRB</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">MET</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">SLBP<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn2-cin-02-223">#</xref></td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">NASP</td><td align=